.TH CSTOOL 1 "Peios" "Capstone" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cstool \- disassemble machine code with Capstone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cstool
.RI [ options ]
.I architecture-mode
.I hexadecimal-code
.RI [ start-address ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cstool
is the command-line frontend for the Capstone multi-architecture disassembly
engine. The architecture and mode are selected by the first operand and the
bytes to disassemble are supplied as an unseparated hexadecimal string.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Enable detailed instruction information.
.TP
.B \-s
Decode undecodable bytes as data (SKIPDATA mode).
.TP
.B \-u
Show immediate operands as unsigned values.
.TP
.B \-v
Show the version and Capstone core build information.
.PP
Run without operands to display the supported architecture-mode combinations.
The optional start address is hexadecimal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B cstool x64 554889e5
.PP
Disassembles an x86-64 function prologue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR objdump (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://www.capstone-engine.org/
